          "id": "745961adac6026986cd4f501a436a3cb968988bd",
          "message": "chore: Apply Postgres best-practice indexing (#6422)\n\n## What\n\n- Updated Stack Overflow Top-K join baselines to use best-practice\nPostgreSQL queries backed by companion B-tree and GIN indexes.\n- Pruned redundant base scan queries and the slow join baseline\n`join_top_k_score_desc_low_selectivity/postgres.sql`.\n- Fixed swapped selectivity tiers for single-table Top-K benchmarks.\n- Cleaned up obsolete references to\n`paradedb.enable_aggregate_late_materialization`.\n\n## Why\n\nPrevious PostgreSQL join baselines used the basescan, which isn't useful\nto compare against.\n\nTop-K joins remain competitive in PostgreSQL when properly indexed,\nwhich makes them interesting to track. But for aggregates ParadeDB is\norders of magnitude faster, and so tracking the Postgres alternative is\nnot worth the CI time.\n\n## How\n\n- Added 4 GIN and 6 B-tree companion indexes to\n`benchmarks/datasets/stackoverflow/indexes/bm25.sql` and\n`benchmarks/datasets/stackoverflow/prewarm.sql` and updated 7 Top-K join\n`postgres.sql` queries to target these companion indexes.\n- Retained representative base scans in `count_filter`,\n`aggregate_topk_count`, `join_aggregate_count`, and\n`cardinality/basescan_distinct.sql`, but otherwise dropped all basescan\naggregates which had native-SQL aggregatescan alternatives.\n\n## Tests\n\nBenchmarks run more than 1h faster.",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-21T13:15:56-07:00",
          "tree_id": "03dd6327053c950d659020846df8903af1b3e874",
