          "distinct": true,
          "id": "be9bd8f71b3163d72601f08297271eb0fef5e92c",
          "message": "perf: Encapsulate visibility checking, and prune ctids as soon as possible (#6442)\n\n## What\n\nEncapsulates CTID fetching and heap visibility checking into\n`VisibilityChecker`, decouples visibility filtering from\n`SegmentedTopKExec`, and prunes unused `ctid_*` columns via embedded\nprojections on `VisibilityFilterExec`.\n\n## Why\n\n- Reduces heap buffer accesses by leveraging the visibility map\nfast-path for all-visible pages in `VisibilityChecker`.\n- Eliminates unnecessary shuffling when ctids are pruned from the query\noutput.\n- Simplifies `SegmentedTopKExec` by removing inlined visibility checks\nand allowing `VisibilityFilterExec` to handle them uniformly.\n\n## How\n\n- `VisibilityChecker::check_segment_docs`: encapsulates visibility\nchecking using the visibility map fast-path. When `is_pruned` is true,\nreturns only a boolean visibility mask without materializing Arrow CTID\narrays; unpruned columns retain CTIDs, with downstream tuple fetching\nresolving any HOT redirects on surviving rows.\n- `SegmentedTopKExec`: stripped of inlined visibility filter execution;\nstandard `VisibilityFilterExec` nodes are placed in the physical plan\ninstead.\n- `VisibilityFilterExec`: gains an optional embedded projection to prune\ncolumns immediately upon filtering, with index-based projection mapping\nin `gather_filters_for_pushdown` for filter pushdown remapping.\n\n## Tests\n\nMany, many regress changes. Benchmarks get marginally faster.",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-23T14:50:39-07:00",
          "tree_id": "ed05b09222c3b1d833e2fbb25d04e45f2691e128",
          "url": "https://github.com/paradedb/paradedb/commit/be9bd8f71b3163d72601f08297271eb0fef5e92c"
