          "id": "d30270ab8761b0dc9568535c0dbd312ca4d57a89",
          "message": "perf: skip obsolete segment probes during reader setup (#6435)\n\n## What\n\nSkip invisible segment entries before checking recyclability when\nopening `Snapshot` and `LargestSegment` readers.\n\n## Why\n\n`load_metas` currently checks whether each deleted segment can be\nrecycled before checking whether the reader can see it. That\nrecyclability check acquires the segment's pin-test buffer and attempts\na conditional cleanup lock, even though these reader modes will reject\nthe entry regardless of the result. Each reader open pays this cost\nagain, including planning-time estimation opens.\n\n## How\n\nAdd an early visibility check for these two reader modes.\nParallel-worker replay retains the existing recyclability checks so it\ncan still resolve retired segments kept alive by the origin reader's\npins. No storage-format change or index rebuild is required.\n\n## Tests",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-24T00:16:52-07:00",
          "tree_id": "7766a075124c6d51996b5a03d980c978586900fe",
          "url": "https://github.com/paradedb/paradedb/commit/d30270ab8761b0dc9568535c0dbd312ca4d57a89"
